Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Fri Oct 16 07:10:49 2026 -0500

    fix: make install.sh PATH block skippable (--no-path + CI/SUDO_USER//tmp auto-skips). Addresses REVIEW-TJ-014.
    
    install.sh unconditionally appended a '# terminal-jail' PATH block to the
    first existing rc file, so scratch-prefix installs (TERMINAL_JAIL_INSTALL_DIR
    under /tmp), CI runs, and sudo runs polluted the caller's real login env.
    
    - New --no-path flag skips the PATH setup block entirely (install still
      completes; the manual export line is still printed). Boolean-style: an
      explicit --no-path=<value> is refused with exit 2, nothing written.
    - Three auto-skips, each with a one-line notice naming the reason, first hit
      wins: SUDO_USER set (rc belongs to the invoking user, not root), CI set to
      a truthy value (0/false/no/off do not count), install prefix under /tmp
      (ephemeral/scratch).
    - --uninstall path and the '# terminal-jail' marker format are unchanged.
    - README Install section documents --no-path and the auto-skip behavior;
      install.sh usage text lists the flag.
    
    Tests: 8 new cases in plugin/test_install.py cover all three skip
    conditions, the flag (skip + value-refusal + --help), skip precedence,
    the CI=0 negative control, and an uninstall-removes-marked-block regression
    guard. RED-proven: reverting only install.sh fails 7 of them against the
    pre-fix installer. Full plugin suite 1838 passed / 8 skipped; uvx ruff clean.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
